Description: modular security hardening tool for Linux
 Lockd applies and audits security hardening measures on Debian and Ubuntu
 systems through self-contained modules: firewall, SSH hardening, kernel
 sysctl tuning, filesystem mount restrictions, SUID auditing and more.
 Modules are grouped into cumulative security levels and reusable profiles.
 .
 All privileged actions run through a single audited helper invoked via
 Polkit, which records every operation to an append-only journal.
 .
 This package provides the engine, the command-line interface, the module
 catalogue and the privileged helper. For the graphical interface install
 lockd-gtk.

Package: lockd-gtk
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         lockd (= ${binary:Version}),
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
         gir1.2-adw-1
Description: modular security hardening tool for Linux - GTK interface
 Lockd applies and audits security hardening measures on Debian and Ubuntu
 systems through self-contained modules grouped into cumulative security
 levels and reusable profiles.
 .
 This package provides the GTK4/libadwaita graphical interface. The engine
 and command-line tools are provided by the lockd package.
